## 0. Pre-registrations (verbatim, with sha256)
# scratch/b41/prereg_split_size.txt sha256 6628b9e32b65e942f18e8ceaac8f813be0e45ac21f92757e130dfea8f36746e5
#   Pre-registration: offline sizing of the shim/MemTile role split (union box on the shim, per-core cut on the MemTile)
#   Written 2026-10-15, Desktop 2, before split_size.py has been run.
#   
#   Design sized: every one-quad activation fill whose four per-core slices form one 3-D box (planes x row span x
#   bytes) when unioned is replaced by that box on the shim; the MemTile cuts the four per-core objects from it
#   (split offsets + dims_to_stream). Consecutive boxes in one column program merge by repeat (merge_runs) up to a
#   cap of k boxes per task (k = 4, 8, 16), standing for the MemTile buffer it holds. Every other fill is unchanged.
#   
#   Priced per layer under the two surviving models (scratch/b36/calib.py constants):
#     A  max(act bytes per column / 6.9 GB/s, 1.42 us x tasks)
#     C  act bytes per column / 6.9 GB/s + 0.372 us x tasks
#   
#   Kill line: if the YOLOv8s saving under model A at k = 8 is under 1.0 ms, stop before any device probe or engine
#   code. Saving under C is reported beside it but does not decide.
#   Validity: the union test must be exact (set equality of byte offsets), and total delivered bytes per core must
#   be unchanged (the MemTile re-cut delivers the same objects).
# scratch/b41/prereg_mtsplit_sit.txt sha256 196d9db80fbd5638bd8a26b297f848cbe4e88727b7d892575c77b6f058e4d2b0
#   Pre-registration: device sitting for the shim/MemTile role split (tools/task_issue_probe.py o4raw / boxraw)
#   Written 2026-10-15, Desktop 2 (Phoenix), before any timing dispatch of these builds. Builds are the non-check
#   variants (cores acquire/release only); exactness was established separately on check builds:
#     1 col x 16 quads: o4 (IRON) 0/409,600 mismatched; o4raw, boxraw k1, boxraw k4 0/409,600.
#     4 col x 64 quads: o4raw k1, boxraw k16, boxraw k64 0/6,553,600.
#     box via IRON split + dims_to_stream: ERT_CMD_STATE_TIMEOUT (child BD len = offset gap 1000/1000/1000/15400,
#     read from the lowered IR); not part of this sitting.
#   
#   What the arms are: per quad (4 cores x 6,400 B) the engine's dominant YOLOv8s fill shape, core j = 4 planes x rows
#   5j..5j+7 x 200 B (3-row overlap between neighbours).
#     o4     IRON ObjectFifo split, cut on the shim, 1 quad per task (the engine's form today).
#     o4raw  same shim tasks, hand-written MemTile/core DMA (relay-lock S2MM chain) - the like-for-like control.
#     boxraw union box (4 x 23 x 200 = 18,400 B per quad, 28% fewer shim bytes) on the shim, k boxes per task by
#            repeat; MemTile MM2S cuts the four 6,400 B objects (dims [4@4600, 8@200, 200@1], offsets 1000 j).
#   
#   Grid (Q = 1024 quads per column; 3 rounds x 30 dispatches, rotated, odd rounds reversed, child per point):
#     4 columns: o4:1, o4raw:1, boxraw:1, boxraw:2, boxraw:8, boxraw:64
#     1 column:  o4raw:1, boxraw:1, boxraw:8
#   
#   Predictions (ms, frame = dispatch; shim transport 6.9 GB/s per column, issue 1.42 us/task serial over the array,
#   C's additive 0.372 us/task; absolute values carry an unmodelled intercept, so the rules below use deltas
#   against o4raw k1 in the same column count):
#     4 col  o4raw k1   tasks 4096, 26.2 MB/col   A max(3.80, 5.82)=5.82        C 3.80+1.52=5.32
#            boxraw k1  tasks 4096, 18.8 MB/col   A 5.82  (delta  0.00)        C 2.73+1.52=4.25 (delta -1.07)
#            boxraw k2  tasks 2048               A 2.91  (delta -2.91)        C 2.73+0.76=3.49 (delta -1.83)
#            boxraw k8  tasks  512               A 2.73  (delta -3.09)        C 2.92            (delta -2.40)
#            boxraw k64 tasks   64               A 2.73  (delta -3.09)        C 2.75            (delta -2.57)
#     1 col  o4raw k1   tasks 1024               A 3.80                       C 4.18
#            boxraw k1                           A 2.73  (delta -1.07)        C 3.11 (delta -1.07)
#            boxraw k8                           A 2.73  (delta -1.07)        C 2.78 (delta -1.40)
#   
#   Decision rules (band 0.15 ms on a mean-of-rounds delta):
#    R1 protocol cost: |o4raw - o4| <= 0.15 at 4 col -> the raw protocol is like-for-like; otherwise report the gap and
#       read every boxraw delta against o4raw only.
#    R2 model: 4-col boxraw k1 - o4raw k1 within 0.15 of 0 -> favours A; within 0.30 of -1.07 -> favours C; otherwise
#       neither ("intermediate", report the fraction of C's byte term that appeared).
#    R3 kill line (frame): re-price scratch/b41/split_size.py's YOLOv8s saving under the favoured model (A 3.27, C 1.81
#       at cap 8). If R2 says neither, scale: projected = A-saving x (measured 4-col k8 delta / A's -3.09). Under 1.0 ms
#       -> stop before engine code. A hang or any mismatch on a later check voids the sitting.
#    R4 the step: 4-col boxraw k2 vs k64 within 0.15 -> merging past 2 boxes buys nothing at this traffic (as the
#       contig grid found for 2+ quads).
#   Only these rules decide; anything else in the log is exploratory.

